# The one pinned NATS server, shared by every path that provisions one.
#
# Before this file there were three strategies and no agreement between them:
# Dockerfile.mono installed Debian's nats-server, deploy/setup.sh downloaded
# whatever the GitHub API called "latest" (falling back to 2.11.3) with no
# checksum at all, and the rpm shipped nothing while only *recommending* a
# package Fedora does not have. Three provisioning paths, three possible
# versions, one of them unverified and installed to /usr/local/bin as root.
#
# Sourceable by bash (deploy/setup.sh) and trivially parsed by Python
# (scripts/build_native_release.py) so neither can drift from the other.
#
# Checksums are upstream's own, from the release's SHA256SUMS asset:
#   https://github.com/nats-io/nats-server/releases/download/v2.14.6/SHA256SUMS
# Bump both the version and the digests together, deliberately — a version bump
# with a stale digest must fail the download, not skip the check.
NATS_VERSION=2.14.6
NATS_SHA256_amd64=61c3d55f69f61ec616b75782250936445f2819e9e5f2ae6159b10a31abd2200c
NATS_SHA256_arm64=3ff6e463762db64186a36cf0276dae8320509e995151ad0153ba9c9f67eee3f9
